<title>LITHUANIA: YIELDS FALL ON SIX-MONTH T-BILLS.</title>
<headline>YIELDS FALL ON SIX-MONTH T-BILLS.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yields fell on six-month</p>
<p>Lithuanian Treasury bills at Tuesday's auction and all of the</p>
<p>50 million litas issue was sold as it was oversubscribed, the</p>
<p>country's central bank said.</p>
<p>The average yield on the 179-day paper was 10.08 percent,</p>
<p>down from the 10.84 percent offered at the last auction with a</p>
<p>similar maturity, for 182-days, on April 15.</p>
<p>The settlement date for the issue is May 5 and the bills</p>
<p>mature on October 31.</p>
<p>All figures in millions of litas:</p>
<p>SOLD  DEMAND  MIN/MAX YIELD  AV. YIELD  LAST AV. YIELD</p>
<p>50    139.945  9.00/10.24	10.08	  10.84</p>
<p>-- Ed Stoddard, Vilnius newsroom +370 2 22 35 18</p>
